This package is still under development. If you find a bug (especially under Windows), or if you have any criticisms/questions about this package, then please feel free to email the package developer.  I am grateful to  Prof Brian Ripley and Sergey Fedorov for reporting bugs and making suggestions that  I have been developing neojags.  Thanks also to Martyn Plummer for developing JAGS, Matthew Denwood for developing runjags, Mikis Stasinopoulos et.al. for developing gamlss.dist


VERSION HISTORY
Version 0.1.8
Compile and link flags are now taken from rjags::pkg.compile.flags(), so neojags is always built against the same JAGS (4.x or 5.x) as rjags; this fixes the installation failure on Windows with JAGS 5 (-ljags-4 not found). Thanks to Matt Denwood
The JAGS maths library is now linked explicitly (-ljrmath on Unix, -ljrmath-0 on Windows), since the distributions call JRmath functions such as jags_lbeta and jags_pgamma
Added GitHub Actions: R CMD check on Linux (JAGS 4 and 5), Windows and macOS, and a release workflow that builds and checks the CRAN tarball for each version tag
Version 0.1.7
Added compatibility and removed version retrictions for JAGS 5.0.0
Version 0.1.4
fixed minor bug

Version 0.1.3

Bugs fixed in latex code for creating pdf
Version 0.1.2

Bug fixed in configure.ac

Version 0.1.1

First release on CRAN
